{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "expand-sourcetype-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.5 step 7d, the SOURCE TYPE dimension at width five: the `expand-sourcetype` run computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE through `moves-onroad.esm`. Source types 11 (motorcycle), 21 (passenger car), 31 (passenger truck), 51 (refuse truck) and 62 (combination long-haul truck) -- two light-duty, one heavy-duty vocational, one long-haul and a motorcycle, which is as far apart as this database's physics gets.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES over `expand-fueltype-diesel`, which is the same axis at width two.\n\n* FORTY DRIVE CYCLES RATHER THAN FOUR, and forty that disagree. A drive cycle is per VEHICLE, and a vehicle is a row of `sourceusetypephysics` -- (sourceTypeID, regClassID, model-year range), with its own rolling, rotating and drag terms, its own mass and its own fixed mass factor. These five source types select 40 of the table's 178 rows: 1 each for the motorcycle and the passenger car, 3 for the passenger truck, 15 for the refuse truck and 20 for the combination long-haul truck. So the vehicle-specific power of a drive-schedule second, the operating mode it bins into and the mode distribution the rates are weighted by differ 40 ways, and `n_physicsRow` is 40 where `expand-fueltype-diesel` needs 4 and every run in `runspecs/` before them needed 1. A motorcycle and a combination long-haul truck do not share an operating-mode distribution, and neither do a refuse truck's fifteen regulatory-class-and-model-year bands.\n\n* A COHORT COUNT THAT IS A SUM OVER FIVE UNEQUAL TERMS. 430 rows: 41 + 125 + 125 + 89 + 50. Source type 11 carries one fuel and 41 model years; 21 and 31 carry four fuels each and reach the full 125; 51 and 62 carry fuels the database has fewer sample vehicles for. 656 candidates in the grid, 430 survivors, and no declaration anywhere says 430 -- `cohortSurvivorCount` recomputes it and `tools/check-runspec-shape.py` holds the emitted relation to it.\n\nTHE TEN SELECTIONS, ONE BINDING AND THE ORACLE are everything this document carries, and it differs from `runspecs/expand-fueltype-diesel.esm` in eleven `url_template`s alone.\n\nWHY THIS DOCUMENT IS IN `runspecs/pending/` AND NOT `runspecs/`, as of 2026-09-19, and for the THIRD distinct reason in three days. It waited on the source bin, then on the physics row, then on a memory ceiling that was upstream and is now fixed -- EarthSciAST #420 and #423, merged 2026-09-19, which took this run from 32 GB and killed to 0.89 GB and 91 seconds (PLAN.md §7.3.8). It evaluates. What it does not do is reproduce, and the gap is now THREE CELLS of 430.\n\nWHAT IS ALREADY PROVEN BY RUNNING IT, which is most of it. 427 of 430 cells are inside the 2e-05 tolerance and the per-pollutant emissionQuant total is exact at 3.890e-07. Forty drive cycles, five source types from a motorcycle to a combination long-haul truck, a refuse truck's fifteen regulatory-class-and-model-year physics bands and a 430-row cohort count that is a sum over five unequal terms -- all of that is right, and none of it could be checked before this document evaluated at all.\n\nWHAT IT WAITS ON: three cells, and they are one thing. Source type 51 (refuse truck), fuel type 9 (electricity), model years 2017, 2018 and 2019, every one of them high by exactly 2.623x. Three things it is NOT, each measured rather than assumed: not the physics-row match, because no (sourceTypeID, regClassID, modelYearID) triple in `sourceusetypephysics` is covered by more than one row anywhere in the table and `run_rateRowsWithoutPhysics` is 0; not the electric-vehicle efficiency, because `evefficiency`'s battery and charging factors are identical across all four of this source type's regulatory classes; and not a bin selection, because the cohort carries exactly ONE bin with a non-zero `stmyFraction` -- regClass 47, engTech 30 -- of the 17 the model year holds, with `run_sourceBinsDropped` 0. A constant ratio on one (source type, fuel type) pair is the signature 7d has met four times already: a key that is plural in the data and singular in the model. PLAN.md §7.3.8.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "expand-day"
    ]
  },
